{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "The legendary Blades of the Heralds, more powerful than ordinary Shardblades.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-3" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Blades of the Heralds, given to them by Honor. They aren't spren, so anyone can use one, and holding one grants Surgebinding without a Nahel bond.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Honorblades, the Blades of the Heralds, are legendary treasures, more powerful than ordinary Shardblades. While one is summoned it changes the colour of its holder's eyes.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-3" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Honorblades were given to the Heralds by Honor. They aren't made from a spren bond, so anyone can use one, and each grants the Surges of its Herald's order.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "In Shinovar",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "106" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Seven of the Honorblades are kept by the Shin, who have guarded them for millennia.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "88" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "The nine abandoned Honorblades ended up in Shinovar.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "106" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The Shin custodians",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "83" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "117" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "90" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Szeth replaced Tuko as the bearer of Jezrien's Blade after his pilgrimage.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "83" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ishar directed the Honorbearers to let Szeth retain the Blade when they declared him Truthless.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "117" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Elid became the bearer of Chanarach's Honorblade.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "90" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Jezrien's Honorblade",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "96" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Szeth uses Jezrien's Honorblade to kill rulers across Roshar between 1167 and 1173, among them Gavilar Kholin, King Hanavanar of Jah Keved and two Prime Aqasixes of Azir.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "During the Battle of Narak Szeth fights Kaladin with it, and at the end he gives up his bond and it ends up in Kaladin's hands.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kaladin passes it to Dalinar, who hides it in Urithiru and then gives it to Kaladin's men for training and for working the Oathgates; they swap it among themselves to keep its holder secret.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "96" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Agents of the Diagram work out when Eth holds it, kill him with a Shardblade and steal it. In time it's given to Leshwi, who passes it to Moash so he can join the Fused in the skies.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Talenel's Honorblade",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "42" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Talenel returns carrying his Honorblade, which doesn't vanish when he drops it. On the way to the Shattered Plains it's swapped for an ordinary Shardblade.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "76" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Shin recovered the Blade, and Rit became its bearer.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "42" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Fighting the Honorbearers",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "141" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Nightblood damaged several Honorblades during Szeth's fight against Ishar's returning Honorbearers.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "141" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Nature of the Honorblades",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "53" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "65" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "89" },
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "144" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Honorblades can talk with Nightblood and remain weapons rather than becoming spren in Shadesmar.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "53" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "They are solid manifestations of Honor's god metal.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "65" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "They anchor the Oathpact and can be corrupted after their Herald dies permanently.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "89" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A new Honorblade can take a form other than a sword: Kaladin's appeared as a spear.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "144" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The Blades",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "16" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-4" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "111" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Heralds carried Blades, each unique and covered in glyphs and patterns. At Aharietiam, the Last Desolation, nine of them left their Blades behind.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anyone can use an Honorblade, not just a Herald; like a Shardblade, it can be bonded, summoned and dismissed.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prologue" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Honorblades are made of Honor's own Investiture, which he splintered off himself and crystallised into metal.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "16" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Unlike Radiant Shardblades, Honorblades can't change shape.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-4" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Honorblades are nearly indestructible.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "111" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Surgebinding",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-1" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "98" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Holding an Honorblade grants the ability to Surgebind without a Nahel bond.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-1" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Using Surges through an Honorblade takes more Stormlight, up to dangerous levels. The Shin still train some of their people to use the Blades and their Surges.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "98" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
